course: dictionary
lesson: 12370
title: Crossways: across, not along
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Crossways is an adverb. It tells you the direction of something: it goes across from one side to the other, not along. Think of a cross: it goes over something at an angle.
explain: «Dad laid the sticks crossways on the fire.» The sticks do not run from the front to the back of the fire. They lie across it, from one side to the other.
explain: Look for clues in the other words. «The path ran crossways over the field, not along the hedge.» The words not along tell you the direction. If you swap in across and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Crossways means across, from one side to the other, not along.
fact: «Ella cut the carrot crossways into round slices.» Each slice is cut across the carrot.
fact: Crossways can also mean placed so that one thing crosses over another, like an X.
fact: Crosswise means the same as crossways.
fact: In US informal speech, «get crossways with someone» means to fall out with them.
exercise: «Dad laid the sticks crossways on the fire.» Which way are the sticks lying? | Underneath the fire | Along the fire, from front to back | *Across the fire, from one side to the other | Standing straight up
exercise: «The path ran crossways over the field, not along the hedge.» What does crossways mean here? | Very fast | *Across, not along | Upwards | Along the hedge
exercise: Which word means the same as crossways? | *crosswise | backwards | slowly
test: «Mum placed the two pencils crossways, like an X.» What shape do the pencils make? | A straight line | A square | A circle | *An X
test: «The rope was tied crossways over the door.» Where does the rope go? | *Across the door | Straight up the wall | Along the door | Under the door
exam: «The fallen tree lay crossways over the stream.» What does crossways mean here? | *Across the stream, from one bank to the other | Far away from the stream | Along the stream | Floating down the stream
